    <div class="ts-card-body">Haman = <em>ge'us</em> from Adam's sin. Shaul's false humility → Agag → Haman. Mordechai: humble yet refused to bow. Dovid: soft as worm in Torah, hard as wood in battle. Purim = Yom ki-Purim = two identical goats = two identical-looking types of <em>azus</em>, only the <em>goral</em> (from Hashem) discerns. <em>Shekalim</em> = <em>tzedakah</em> = the great scale: <em>machatzis hashekel</em> = poised between humility and holy boldness.</div>
